Package: sconjoint
Title: Structural Random-Utility Estimation for Conjoint Experiments
Version: 0.4.3
Date: 2026-11-27
Authors@R: c(
    person("Avidit", "Acharya", role = "aut"),
    person("Jens", "Hainmueller", role = "aut"),
    person("Yiqing", "Xu", , "yiqingxu@stanford.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Estimates a structural random-utility model for forced-choice
    conjoint experiments. Repeated choices by the same respondent separate
    persistent tastes from task-level shocks and a respondent-specific
    position (side) preference. Tastes follow a normal law with a low-rank
    covariance (q taste factors); a neural network links mean tastes to
    respondent characteristics. Estimation uses respondent-level
    cross-fitting and score correction for specified population means,
    preference shares, contrasts, average marginal effects, expected support
    in hypothetical matchups, and the decisiveness of named attribute swaps.
    Inference rests on the model and stated regularity conditions. Attribute
    importance is descriptive. Individual posterior summaries condition on
    fitted population parameters.
